{"id":"la-madeleine","name":"La Madeleine","qid":"Q330564","country":"France","locality":"8th arrondissement of Paris","lat":"48.87","lon":"2.324444444","built":"1845","year":1845,"year_text":"1845","century":"19th century","era":"19th century","period":"","date_basis":"Wikidata, inception","style":"Neoclassical architecture","heritage":"classified historical monument","type":"church building","wikipedia":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/La_Madeleine,_Paris","text":"The Church of Saint Mary Magdalene (French: église Sainte-Marie-Madeleine [eɡliz sɛ̃t maʁi madlɛn]), less formally called La Madeleine ([la madlɛn]), is a Catholic parish church on Place de la Madeleine in the eighth arrondissement of Paris. It was planned by Louis XV as the focal point of the new Rue Royal, leading to the new Place Louis XV, the present Place de la Concorde. It was dedicated in 1764 by Louis XV, but work was halted due to the French Revolution.","text_source":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/La_Madeleine,_Paris","text_license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","real":[{"id":"gh-1e310bce4215","w":1200,"h":674,"title":"Église de la Madeleine 1, Paris July 2011.jpg","o":"gh-1e310bce4215.jpg","credit":{"text":"Joe deSousa","license":"CC BY 2.0","license_url":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/2.0","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%C3%89glise_de_la_Madeleine_1%2C_Paris_July_2011.jpg","via":"Wikimedia Commons"}},{"id":"gh-4afa509340b5","w":1200,"h":800,"title":"Eglise de la Madeleine 2024.jpg","o":"gh-4afa509340b5.jpg","credit":{"text":"Callaway Kosine – de Suzannet","license":"CC BY 3.0","license_url":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/3.0","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Eglise_de_la_Madeleine_2024.jpg","via":"Wikimedia Commons"}},{"id":"gh-4d7a371495f2","w":1200,"h":887,"title":"Église Madeleine - Paris VIII (FR75) - 2025-10-07 - 3.jpg","o":"gh-4d7a371495f2.jpg","credit":{"text":"Chabe01","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","license_url":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/b